Fix library focus on EGLFS when QApplication::focusWindow() is null
or reports stale/hidden popup windows.

On EGLFS embedded platforms (Mali GPU, no window manager),
focusWindow() can be null at startup and after QComboBox popups
close. A hidden/closed popup may still be reported as focusWindow(),
permanently locking focus to ContextMenu. Re-opening a cached
popup may resist Escape key on EGLFS.

Four changes:
1. setLibraryFocus: Instead of bailing out when focusWindow() is null,
   try requestActivate() but proceed with widget focus regardless.
2. emitKeyEvent: Instead of bailing out when focusWindow() is null,
   fall through to send key events directly to the library view when
   no focus widget is available.
3. getFocusedWidget: When focusWindow() is null, check if any library
   widget has focus before returning None. When focusWindow() is Popup
   but hidden, return None instead of ContextMenu.
4. slotMoveVertical: ContextMenu case sends Escape then force-closes
   via activePopupWidget() (for cached/re-opened popups on EGLFS),
   reclaims library focus, and falls through to scroll. None case
   also falls through to scroll instead of returning early.

This is safe on EGLFS because MIXXX is the only application; the
browse encoder should always scroll the library.

